      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Polish quota warning settings",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n- Redesign global quota warning settings into compact Session/Weekly threshold rows.\r\n- Remove the Apply button and noisy row separators.\r\n- Add `%` labels and reorder thresholds as Lower then Higher.\r\n- Dim disabled quota warning rows while preserving saved threshold values.\r\n- Save edited thresholds on Return, focus loss, outside click, or view teardown instead of every keystroke.\r\n- Fix the Higher field focus/loading issue by anchoring outside-click detection to the threshold editor bounds.\r\n- Ignore unchanged threshold saves to avoid unnecessary refresh churn.\r\n- Update “Upper” localization copy to “Higher” equivalents across resource catalogs.\r\n\r\n## Why\r\nThe previous settings layout could wrap and misalign inside macOS SwiftUI `Form`, making the quota warning section feel buggy. Saving every keystroke also caused unnecessary provider refresh behavior while users were still editing. This makes the layout cleaner, the editing flow calmer, and the focus/save behavior more reliable.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n- `swift test --filter SettingsStoreTests`\r\n- `swift test --filter PreferencesPaneSmokeTests`\r\n- `make check`\r\n\r\n## Screenshot\r\n### before\r\n<img width=\"600\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-07 at 9 33 30 AM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2ebaccfb-11f2-4d58-a7fd-5b32f3575681\" />\r\n\r\n### after\r\n<img width=\"600\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-07-07 at 3 07 46 PM\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/97ea7dd2-3e89-4306-b42d-411751a73e0f\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\nProvider-specific quota warning layout polish is intentionally left for a follow-up PR.",
